  <name>SMTP JS API CC/BCC Test Channel</name>
  <description>NET-10 / SC-3 (18.5-05, PR-#177-GATED): Channel Reader (REST-pumped) source + ONE JavaScript Writer destination whose Rhino script calls the userutil SMTPConnection API (SMTPConnectionFactory.createSMTPConnection(), host/port overridden to 127.0.0.1:${SMTP_JS_PORT}) in three arities selected by the incoming HL7 PID last name (extracted into channelMap.patientName by the existing transformer step): the new 7-arg send(to,cc,bcc,from,subject,body,charset) that PR #177 adds (D1), and the pre-existing legacy 6-arg send(to,cc,from,subject,body,charset) (D2) / 5-arg send(to,cc,from,subject,body) (D3) overloads, which must keep delivering unchanged. All three send(...) calls live ONLY inside this Rhino script string -- never referenced from compiled Java anywhere in smoke-tests -- so this channel deploys cleanly and the smoke-tests build compiles on the current branch even though the 7-arg overload does not exist yet (Pitfall 1). SmtpJsApiCcBccTest's @BeforeClass Assume-gates the whole class on -DPR177_PRESENT, so this channel is deployed but never pumped while PR #177 is absent. Distinct-domain throwaway mailboxes (to.smoke.test/cc.smoke.test/bcc.smoke.test/from.smoke.test) on a DEDICATED SmtpStub (SMTP_JS_PORT) -- never the SMTP_CCBCC_PORT stub from smtp-ccbcc-test.xml (Pitfall 3). Test-only; never deploy to production.</description>
